> aren't really worth the difference in AC to me.  It would be a
> temptation not a solution.  Do added temptations add game balance?  Not
> to well spoiled or well experienced players and I think most of the
> discussion here is intended to address them not beginners.

It depends on what other changes to MC are made.  In vanilla 3.4.3,
MC3 is already so close to 100% protection that going beyond it
wouldn't really make much difference.

But this thread was originally about reducing the effectiveness of MC
in general (among other things).  If MC was nerfed so that, say, two
MC3 layers gave about the same protection as plain MC3 currently does,
while a single MC3 layer acted like something between MC1 and MC2
currently, then the difference might well be worth a few AC points.

Especially if you happened to be playing a well prepared combat wombat
with more than enough HP and AC anyway.

(Just for reference, the base AC difference between mithril and DSM is
3 points for dwarvish mithril and 4 for elven.  Elven mithril can be
safely enchanted to +7, reducing the gap to 2 points at maximum safe
enchantment.)

In fact, I could imagine some situations where mithril plus an MC1/2
cloak could be worthwhile even in vanilla, except that all the cloaks
worth wearing are MC3 anyway.  (And no, I don't consider displacement
worth wearing if there's anything better to be had, but let's not
start that thread again.)

